          "answer": 0,
          "answerIndex": 0,
          "why": "SSI tracks read-write dependencies using lightweight in-memory SIREAD flags. When adjacent rw-antidependencies form a cycle in the dependency graph, the engine aborts a transaction with 40001 to maintain serializability.",
          "explanation": "SSI tracks read-write dependencies using lightweight in-memory SIREAD flags. When adjacent rw-antidependencies form a cycle in the dependency graph, the engine aborts a transaction with 40001 to maintain serializability."
