        "example": "Imagine a multinational banking consortium with headquarters in New York and branch vaults in London and Tokyo. In an ad-hoc system, a New York teller must place international telephone calls to Tokyo clerks for every transaction, waiting on hold for hours. Under Foreign Data Wrappers (SQL/MED), the New York headquarters installs dedicated, authenticated fiber-optic telecommunication conduits directly into the Tokyo vault ledger. When a New York teller queries an account, the secure terminal automatically fetches the remote Tokyo ledger record in milliseconds as if it were stored in the next room.",
        "code": "-- Configuring Foreign Data Wrapper (postgres_fdw) Server Definitions and User Mappings\nCREATE TABLE fdw_configuration_matrix (\n    configuration_element TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n    sql_command_syntax TEXT,\n    security_scope_profile TEXT,\n    performance_optimization_role TEXT,\n    production_resiliency_impact TEXT\n);\nINSERT INTO fdw_configuration_matrix VALUES\n('Extension Installation', 'CREATE EXTENSION postgres_fdw', 'System Catalog Handler Registration', 'Registers validator and planner callback hooks', 'Prerequisite for all distributed foreign table operations'),\n('Foreign Server Definition', 'CREATE SERVER shard_node_01 FOREIGN DATA WRAPPER ...', 'Host and Port Network Isolation', 'keep_connections = on avoids repeated TCP/TLS handshakes', 'Defines network target, socket timeouts, and fetch batch sizes'),\n('User Mapping Authorization', 'CREATE USER MAPPING FOR user SERVER ...', 'Role-Based Credential Isolation', 'Binds local roles to secure remote worker accounts', 'Prevents privilege escalation and isolates database roles'),\n('Foreign Table Declaration', 'CREATE FOREIGN TABLE ... SERVER shard_node_01 ...', 'Transparent Virtual Schema Definition', 'Directs SQL queries to remote physical relation', 'Provides uniform local table interface over remote network storage');\n\nSELECT \n    configuration_element,\n    sql_command_syntax,\n    performance_optimization_role,\n    production_resiliency_impact\nFROM fdw_configuration_matrix\nORDER BY configuration_element;",
