        "example": "Imagine an express coffee barista serving commuter customers. For the first five customers who order a personalized hazelnut oat latte with extra foam, the barista carefully crafts each cup by hand, measuring syrups and milk temperatures individually (Custom Plans). By the sixth customer, the barista recognizes that eighty percent of commuters order a standard medium cappuccino; the barista pre-brews a batch carafe (Generic Plan) that serves future commuters in two seconds flat. If a customer arrives asking for an ultra-rare triple-temperature pour-over, the barista steps aside to brew a custom single cup.",
        "code": "-- Inspecting Prepared Statement Lifecycle, Five-Execution Rule, and Plan Caching Mechanics\nCREATE TABLE prepared_statement_lifecycle_mechanics (\n    execution_phase TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n    planner_strategy_used TEXT,\n    plan_caching_behavior TEXT,\n    cpu_optimization_impact TEXT,\n    parameter_binding_nature TEXT\n);\nINSERT INTO prepared_statement_lifecycle_mechanics VALUES\n('Executions 1 through 5', 'Custom Query Plans', 'Plans generated individually using actual parameter values', 'Incurs full planning CPU latency per execution', 'Optimal paths tailored to literal parameter values'),\n('Execution 6 onwards (Default)', 'Heuristic Cost Comparison', 'Compares average custom plan cost against generic plan cost', 'Reuses cached generic plan if within cost tolerance', 'Bound to parameter type placeholders without literal sniffing'),\n('Plan Cache Eviction / Reset', 'Automatic Invalidation', 'Discarded upon schema DDL, index changes, or session exit', 'Zero memory leaks across connection lifecycles', 'Parameters rebound upon subsequent PREPARE invocations');\n\nSELECT \n    execution_phase,\n    planner_strategy_used,\n    plan_caching_behavior,\n    cpu_optimization_impact\nFROM prepared_statement_lifecycle_mechanics\nORDER BY execution_phase;",
